<step1>
<ptxt>How to Use Diagnostic Tool TaSCAN</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>Connecting to the Vehicle</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="D101814J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<step3>
<ptxt>Connect TaSCAN to the DLC3 (data link connector No.3) located near the driver side footwell.</ptxt>
</step3>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>How to Use Diagnostic Tool TaSCAN</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="D031282" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<step3>
<ptxt>When the power switch of the TaSCAN diagnostic tool is turned ON, the menu screen is displayed.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>Select the desired item, then proceed according to the instructions on the screen.</ptxt>
</step3>
</step2>
</step1>
<step1>
<ptxt>Time-series Freeze Data (Using TaSCAN)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="D031290J01" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Time-series freeze data freezes the data at the DTC detection point and before and after it. The frozen data allows the vehicle driving condition (acceleration, deceleration, steady driving, shifting) and the driver's operation status to be accurately checked, which is useful for troubleshooting. It can also be used as data when performing a reproduction test.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>By checking changes in input signals, abnormalities such as momentary interruptions can also be detected.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<step2>
<ptxt>Connect TaSCAN to the DLC3.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Display the [Diagnosis] → [Freeze Data] screen and select the data items.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>After selecting the items, check the data at each point.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="D031291J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</step2>
</step1>
